  "_about": "THE SHRINKING OFFENDER LIST for `make docs-audit`'s `identifier spelling` row, markdown half (D280's pattern; owner's ruling, test-audit plan, 2026-09-27: \"Shrinking offender list now\"). files: file -> lane (who owes the fix) and SPELLING -> entries. An entry is the British word itself, lower-cased, one per occurrence (a word twice in one file is listed twice). A decision entry is keyed by its file tail (docs/decisions/*-<slug>.md, scripts/ste_measure.py:list_key), so a claim that numbers it moves nothing. The row FAILS on a British word this list does not name, on an entry that matches nothing now (stale: delete it), and on an entry the list at the merge-base with origin/main did not hold (growth), unless its rule is not in `rules` at the merge-base. A new file starts clean. `make offenders-prune` deletes stale entries and never adds one. Never add an entry to excuse new prose: the write-time STE hook and this row both exist so new markdown is American from the moment it is written. `docs/gates/` is excluded outright, never listed here.",
